      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The urge to give up when facing the final blankness is a very natural response to that deep despair. If the focus is relentlessly on the end, the struggle can feel meaningless. Perhaps the value can be found not in the \"end result,\" but in the immediate, present moment of the struggle itself. These small, self-willed efforts can feel meaningful right now, independent of the far-off final outcome.",
      "source": "target",
